        headingEn: 'Education in Canada is organised by province',
        bodyEn:
          'Canada does not have a single national ministry that runs university admissions. Education is the responsibility of each province and territory, so the way you apply — and sometimes what you need — varies by where the university is located.\n\nMost provinces have students apply directly to each university. Ontario is the notable exception: applicants there generally use a centralized service called the Ontario Universities\' Application Centre (OUAC). Because of these differences, always check the rules on the official website of each university and its provincial application service.',
