          'This guide explains, in plain language, how working while studying generally works for international students in Canada, using official Government of Canada (IRCC) facts. It is general information only and is not immigration advice.\n\nWork rules for study-permit holders are set by IRCC and have changed in recent years. Whether you can work, how many hours, and on what conditions depend on your specific study permit and your situation. Always confirm the current rules on the official Government of Canada source before you start any job.',
